comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T10:00:00.820Z","harness:claude-code","Root cause located (2026-11-07, while fixing a Codex review finding on the pm-gh1665/1666/1667 batch): wrapProgramActionsForExtensionHandlers in src/cli/main.ts wraps every Commander action and calls runActiveCommandHandler for a registered extension handler BEFORE the dynamic command action runs. validateDynamicExtensionCommandOptions lives only in that dynamic action (runRequiredExtensionCommand), so for a handler-backed command it is never reached. A command with declared flags is still guarded because extractCommandScopedOptions validates loose options against its definitions; a command with no flags is not. The batch PR closes only the root-only subset (--all/--explain) for every extension command, via refuseUndeclaredRootOnlyOptions in the wrapper. The general fix (call the zero-flag option validator in the wrapper) is deliberately left here: it can break packages whose handlers read options they never declared through registerFlags, so it needs a fleet census of package commands that read context.options without declarations, and a migration note.\n"
body: ""
